	Select several with J, K or v, then x completes them all and gG groups them.
	Add a block with o below, O above, i or I inside, a or A at the end or start of the list, then s, p, t or n for a section, project, task or note.
	Make a line of text a section with S, and plain text again with s.
	Color a block with c1 to c6, red to violet, cycle colors with cc, pick one with mc, and remove it with C.
	While editing, start a line with - and a space for a task or end it with : for a project, and Backspace at its start or Delete at its end makes it text again.
	While editing, type / for this block's commands and filter them as you type, as in /due or /color, then Enter.
	Open Today from the sidebar with Alt+0, then j and Enter, for what is due or started by today; Alt+l or gz on one of its blocks goes to it in the outline.
	Find any command by name with Ctrl+K or :, such as Count Blocks and Words for what is under the focused block, or Save As to keep this file somewhere of your own.
	Icons need a Nerd Font: if they show as boxes, set icons = "none" in ~/.config/taskpaper-terminal/config.toml.
	The mouse works too: click a block, the count of its folded children, a crumb or a sidebar entry, Alt+click to open it in a new pane, right-click for its menu.
